<title>MEXICO: Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Bondes rate rises slightly at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican government 728-day development bonds, or Bondes, rose 0.11 percentage points to 1.86 percent above the 28-day Cetes rate in Tuesday's primary auction, dealers estimated.</p>
<p>The 728-day Bondes were assigned at 97.22856 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the Bondes was 1.91 billion pesos, compared with the 800 million offered by the Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559</p>
